description:
*What*
Emit an event when sync is ready
*Why*
Since the horizontal scaling changes to sync, it is a requirement that sync can connect directly to mongodb (no longer using fh.db calls that abstract away mongo and its connection).
Because of this, it is possible that sync may not be ready to handle `sync.init` calls on the server.
There needs to be a way to safely call `sync.init` on the server, knowing that the sync server is ready.
This is not an issue for clients making sync requests as they will likely fail while sync is initialising, then resend their request in the next sync loop (pending updates marked as crashed).
*How*
Having a 'sync_ready' event emitted by fh-mbaas-api ($fh) should suffice for this scenario e.g.
{noformat}
mbaasApi.once('sync_ready', function initDatasets() {
 mbaasApi.sync.init('workorders', syncOptions);
});
{noformat}

