description:
*Why*
One of the value adds of the MCP is to show an overview of each service. This is information that gives you a snap shot view of the service.
*How*
We will want a standard endpoint something like /sys/info/stats and understand the format that we want to return from that endpoint. Do we want a standard format something like :
{code}
{ 
 "some_metric":{
 "metric":{
  "label":"This is a human readable label",
  "value":42
 }
 }
}
{code}
Or allow a custom response type.
* Gather a history (max 1hr) of these responses and store them to allow a view over time, which would mean gathering them on the serverside rather than directly from the service. This would also allow for a situation where the service has "gone away" or is unreachable.
* We would still have a set of metrics plus the knowledge that the service had become unavailable. 
* The API Server should be the thing that gathers the stats for any services. If the service is unavailable, the API server can send back an appropriate response.
* The MCP UI should show all this information to developers

